    "title": {
      "en": "Blizzard Teases Possible Change to Unlock Level of Dual Spec in WoW: Forever",
      "es": "Blizzard se burla de un posible cambio para desbloquear el nivel de especificaciones duales en WoW: Forever"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Blizzard Teases Possible Change to Unlock Level of Dual Spec in WoW: Forever...",
      "es": "Blizzard se burla de un posible cambio para desbloquear el nivel de especificaciones duales en WoW: Forever..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6acc191d90e174.53321197\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">In this week's WoW: Forever podcast, Blizzard teases that they are looking at changing when dual spec unlocks!<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a class=\"wh-button zam-button\" href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/the-wow-forever-podcast-episode-3-now-available-dungeons-and-questing-383309\" data-style=\"cta\" data-variation=\"undefined\"><span class=\"wh-button-text body-text zam-button-text\" data-text-style=\"body-small-bold\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">WoW: Forever Podcast - Ep. 3</span></a></div><br><br>During <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/the-wow-forever-podcast-episode-3-now-available-dungeons-and-questing-383309\" data-contiguous=\"true\">this week's WoW: Forever Podcast</a>, the team was discussing tanks and whether or not you should need a Tank-specific talent build in order to do dungeons. During this time, Josh Greenfield brought up how Dual Spec unlocks at level 40 \"currently\":<div class=\"quote-box exclude-units\" data-type=\"user\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\">Josh Greenfield<span class=\"quote-said-text\"> said: </span></div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">[...] one of the benefits we have is having dual spec, which will come online at th... at level 40 currently. We're talking about what the right level for that to actually enable is, but currently it's set to 40.</div></div><div class=\"quote-box exclude-units\" data-type=\"user\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\">Josh Greenfield<span class=\"quote-said-text\"> said: </span></div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Maybe a cheeky thirty, I don't know, we'll see.</div></div>Unlocking dual spec earlier would allow players to have a separate talent build for dungeons, especially for roles that you may not want to quest in, so having it earlier would be a welcome change for many players.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>In this week's WoW: Forever podcast, Blizzard teases that they are looking at changing when dual spec unlocks!<br /><br />WoW: Forever Podcast - Ep. 3<br /><br />During <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/the-wow-forever-podcast-episode-3-now-available-dungeons-and-questing-383309\">this week's WoW: Forever Podcast</a>, the team was discussing tanks and whether or not you should need a Tank-specific talent build in order to do dungeons. During this time, Josh Greenfield brought up how Dual Spec unlocks at level 40 &quot;currently&quot;:<br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\"><h2 class=\"heading-size-2\">Josh Greenfield</h2> one of the benefits we have is having dual spec, which will come online at th... at level 40 currently. We're talking about what the right level for that to actually enable is, but currently it's set to 40. </div><br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\"><h2 class=\"heading-size-2\">Josh Greenfield</h2>Maybe a cheeky thirty, I don't know, we'll see. </div><br /><br />Unlocking dual spec earlier would allow players to have a separate talent build for dungeons, especially for roles that you may not want to quest in, so having it earlier would be a welcome change for many players.</noscript>            \n        ",
